 "doc_changes": [
  {
   "path": "layouts[0]._start_doc",
   "old": "Ledger 0047's declared start, as vertices into data/centerline.local.json (its own index space: local v0 = the pylons). line_vertex 0 = AC_TIME_0 at the pylons. Forward grid v14417 = 27.0 m behind the line on 19th St; reverse grid v26 = 26.0 m behind it on Lookout Mountain Rd (layout_dummies: 0 < d <= 35 m). Sectors on straight vertices (kink < 1 deg over +/-6 vertices): v7185 near the summit (st 7187.3) and v11623 on US-40 just before exit 259 (st 16564.0), so the three sectors are the climb, the top + canyon, and Golden. Validated 2026-10-11 by tools/layout_dummies.py on a plan-only projection of this centreline; re-run on the real centerline.local.json in P4. offset_right_m 1.6 = the right-hand lane's centre on a ~6.5 m two-lane road, PROVISIONAL: the width at the pylons is not measured (dossier 12). With layout_dummies' +/-1.0 m grid stagger the outer column's car edge sits 3.55 m right of centre, past the edge of a 6.5 m road; re-set it from the aerial width (or single-file the grid) in P4.",
   "new": "Ledger 0047's declared start, as vertices into data/centerline.local.json (its own index space: local v0 = the pylons). line_vertex 0 = AC_TIME_0 at the pylons. Forward grid v14611 = 27.0 m behind the line on 19th St; reverse grid v26 = 26.0 m behind it on Lookout Mountain Rd (layout_dummies: 0 < d <= 35 m). Sectors on straight vertices (kink < 1 deg over +/-6 vertices): v7185 near the summit (st 7186.9) and v11647 on US-40 just before exit 259 (st 16548.0), so the three sectors are the climb, the top + canyon, and Golden. Validated 2026-10-11 by tools/layout_dummies.py on a plan-only projection of this centreline; re-run on the real centerline.local.json in P4. offset_right_m 1.6 = the right-hand lane's centre on a ~6.5 m two-lane road, PROVISIONAL: the width at the pylons is not measured (dossier 12). With layout_dummies' +/-1.0 m grid stagger the outer column's car edge sits 3.55 m right of centre, past the edge of a 6.5 m road; re-set it from the aerial width (or single-file the grid) in P4."
  },
  {
   "path": "race.corridor._boxes_doc",
   "old": "Kevin's 'Corners the race turns at': the full intersection drivable, the legs the race doesn't take sealed at the box edge; the clockwise race uses the same boxes turned the other way. apex = the corner vertex on the V3 centreline (centerline.local.json index); i / j = apex -/+ ~24 m (8 vertices on the 3 m OSM line; re-derived by station onto the paint centreline, where C12 sits on 1 m points and its i / j are 24-25 vertices out), PROVISIONAL until P3b authors the junction mouths and the box edges come from their footprint. C16 spans both junction nodes (v12862, v12867). C17 (the US-6 diverge) is a gore, not a box.",
   "new": "Kevin's 'Corners the race turns at': the full intersection drivable, the legs the race doesn't take sealed at the box edge; the clockwise race uses the same boxes turned the other way. apex = the corner vertex on the V3 centreline (centerline.local.json index); i / j = apex -/+ ~24 m (8 vertices on the 3 m OSM line; re-derived by station onto the paint centreline, where C12 sits on 1 m points and its i / j are 24-25 vertices out), PROVISIONAL until P3b authors the junction mouths and the box edges come from their footprint. C16 spans both junction nodes (v12966, v12978). C17 (the US-6 diverge) is a gore, not a box."
  }
